(a) Upon receipt of a claim from a person, business or other entity seeking damages for personal injury or property damage resulting from the alleged intentional or negligent misconduct of the city or its agents and employees, which is filed or submitted to the city in accord with O.C.G.A. § 36-33-5, such claim shall be immediately transmitted to the city manager of the city for investigation and consideration. Upon the completion of such investigation, in the event that the city manager determines that administrative adjustment or settlement of such claim is in the best interest of the city, he shall be authorized to administratively adjust or settle such claim with the claimant on behalf of the city, upon the following terms and conditions:
(1) Neither the claim itself, nor the administrative adjustment or settlement thereof, shall exceed the sum of $1,000.00;
(2) Only claims for personal injury or property damage resulting from the alleged intentional or negligent misconduct by the city or its agents or employees, while acting in the course of their employment with the city, shall be subject to settlement pursuant to this section;
(3) Prior to entering into the settlement of such claim in accord with the provisions hereof, the city manager shall determine that administrative adjustment or settlement of such claim is in the best interest of the city, will not work an economic or other hardship to the city, that the claim is meritorious, and that further unnecessary delay in settling such claim would be detrimental to the city;
(4) Prior to settlement, the amount claimed by the claimant shall be documented to the satisfaction of the city manager in writing, and the city manager shall not be authorized to settle such claim without such documentation in an amount at least equal to the amount of the final settlement;
(5) The payment of all settlement proceeds shall be paid from funds previously appropriated by the city council of the town in the city's budget for the current fiscal year for the payment of such claims;
(6) Prior to actual payment of the claim, the city manager shall require the claimant to execute a full and final release in favor of the city, its agents, employees, insurance carriers and any other person or entity who might potentially be liable to the claimant as a result of such claim. Such release shall also provide specifically that such release shall not be considered as an admission of any liability to the claimant by any of the releases named or referred to in the release documents;
(7) Any and all documents required to be executed effecting such settlement shall be prepared and approved by the city attorney prior to the execution thereof and the payment of any funds pursuant thereto;
(8) All such settlements shall be made within 30 days of receipt of the claim by the city, unless circumstances beyond the control of the city manager require a longer period of time, in which case, such shall be reported to the city council.
(b) The city manager shall notify the city council as soon as possible, but not to exceed 15 days within the date of the completion of such administrative adjustment or settlement, of the fact of adjustment or settlement and shall further maintain complete and accurate records in his office of all such matters.
(c) Nothing herein shall serve to extend or shorten any statutes of limitation which may be now or hereafter applicable to any claims or claimant herein described. In addition thereto, nothing herein shall be construed as an attempt to alter, amend, change or abrogate the general provisions of state law requiring the filing of ante litum notice (O.C.G.A. § 36-33-6) with the city prior to the filing of suit against the city. Further, the provisions hereof shall not be construed as in any manner changing the official or officials of the city upon whom such ante litum notice or any civil action wherein the city is a named defendant is to be served in accord with state law.
(d) Nothing contained herein shall be construed to prohibit or otherwise limit the authority of the city council from settling or otherwise resolving claims filed against the city in any other manner not provided for in this section.
(Code 1986, § 2-13; Ord. No. O-87-08-17, §§ 1—4, 8-24-1987; Ord. No. O-2015-15, 7-23-2015)

