With regard to purchasing supplies, goods, services and equipment to be utilized or undertaken by or on behalf of the city, it shall be the policy of the city:
(1) To secure the best reasonable price for all supplies, goods, services and equipment consistent with the fiduciary role of the city;
(2) To secure competitive bids whenever such competitive bidding would be in the best interest of the city or whenever it is anticipated that the goods and service to be purchased will exceed $10,000.00 in costs to the city; however, competitive bidding shall not be required either where the goods and services to be purchased are provided only by a sole source otherwise meeting the other requirements of this section, or where goods and service previously purchased can be serviced, updated, upgraded, or repaired only by a sole source otherwise meeting the requirements of this section;
(3) To purchase from vendors located within the city, whenever the price is the lowest reasonable price, or whenever the price differential is no more than five percent of the total or $300.00, whichever is less; provided, however, in the event that there are no vendors located within the city which meet such price differential, then to purchase from vendors located within the county whenever the price is the lowest reasonable price or whenever the price differential is no more than five percent of the total or $300.00, whichever is less;
(4) To use the purchasing division of the department of administrative services of the state whenever it would be in the best interest of the city to do so;
(5) To award a contract for supplies, goods, services or equipment to the lowest responsible bidder whose bid is consistent with the quality, specifications and requirements of the city with respect to the particular supplies, goods, services or equipment bid upon.
(Code 1986, § 10-2; Ord. No. O-88-07-25, 7-25-1988; Ord. No. O-00-04-21, 4-20-2000; Ord. No. O-04-12-32, 12-16-2004)

